{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Pocky-l/diegesis/main/docs/schema/scene.schema.json",
  "$comment": "Farmer's Delight's skillet faces the way its placer looked, so its handle points back at them (+z here): the camera stands on the handle's side, where a cook holds it. While somebody works at it the block's own model is hidden and pan_body, handle (and stand on a campfire) draw it, exactly Farmer's Delight's parts, so the pan can be tossed. pan is the pivot everything in the pan rides on: the fat under the food (oil, painted), the food pieces (piece_N, with under_N for a fuller pan) and lift_N, ghosts of what leaves it. mouth catches stacks let go over the pan, food the clicks of an empty hand, handle the toss; the handle is the only thing with a look that the cursor can hit, so the hover outline marks it alone. book_open is the recipe book, on the left, hung in front of the pan towards the camera as at the board.",
